(Part is a steering knuckle — a suspension/drivetrain component subjected to high cyclic loads. Combined with the cast_and_machine forced process) Tj
T* (and 200,000 units/year volume, this profile matches standard automotive practice: sand or high-pressure sand-moulded ductile iron casting followed by) Tj
T* (CNC finish machining of bores and mating faces. Ductile iron offers the strength/fatigue performance needed for a knuckle at a fraction of steel forging) Tj
T* (cost, and is far more consistent with the wall-thickness/undercut profile here than aluminium \(no HPDC-thin-wall or lightweighting signal present\).) Tj
