(This is a right-hand steering knuckle — a safety-critical suspension component. The sparse fill ratio \(0.0615\) combined with thick,) Tj
T* (non-uniform walls \(1.36–46.75mm\), 52 undercuts, and a mix of cylindrical bores/bosses \(bearing seat, ball-joint and tie-rod bores\) is fully) Tj
T* (consistent with a near-net sand-cast ductile-iron part that is subsequently CNC-machined on 3 setups to finish bores, mounting pads and) Tj
T* (threaded holes. Given the load-bearing, drivetrain-adjacent nature of the part and no aluminium/thin-wall HPDC signal, ductile iron) Tj
T* (\(GJS500/600\) is recommended over aluminium, in line with real-world steering knuckle production practice. At 200,000 units/year,) Tj
T* (high-throughput green-sand or shell-moulding lines with a durable metal pattern \(£17k\) are economically favoured over die costs for) Tj
T* (HPDC/forging.) Tj
